\f1\fs26 Sarah jumped when she heard something like a metal bucket falling down stairs. Alarm planted her hand firmly on Cracker\'92s thigh. His burns made him wince.\
\'93What was that?\'94 Sarah hissed.\
\'93A metal bucket falling down stairs.\'94 Cracker took Sarah\'92s hand and was on his feet. \'93Someone is coming up the fire stairs, someone who doesn\'92t know to avoid the bucket. We gotta go.\'94\
Cracker clunked the front door open and dragged Sarah down the narrow corridor. They heard the fire door open before they reached the elevator lobby. A huge, square-headed shadow blocked their escape.\
\'93You!\'94 the shadow spat.\
\'93You!\'94 Sarah spat back, recognising the agent from Travis Teh\'92s office. Now it was her turn to drag Cracker down a corridor, back to his apartment.\
\'93What\'92s that ape want with you?\'94 Cracker demanded once they were back in the apartment. He leant back against the front door, as if that would baricade it, and glared at Sarah.\
\'93Me? He wants you, you idiot!\'94 Sarah stomped around the living area hoping one of the miserable windows would open up and offer a rainbow bridge to freedom. \'93That\'92s the PAPER agent I warned you about.\'94\
Cracker screwed his face up, confused.\
Sarah stopped pacing. \'93Before the bombing! I came to warn you, remember?\'94\
To Cracker, before the bombing was an age ago.\
\'93Open up!\'94 Three blunt, fist-sized thumps shook through the door. \'93You will return what you stole.\'94\
Sarah pulled a tablet from her bag and went to the apartment\'92s security console in the kitchen. She made a series of frenzied erratic gestures at the tablet. \'93Come on!\'94 she told the tablet. More gestures. \'93He\'92ll be requesting your door unlocks, which it will if I can\'92t subvert the command in time.\'94\
Cracker, with heart belting at the cage of his ribs, stood at the kitchen doorway, and watched Sarah work.\
