Agent Jones pinned Cracker to the couch with a knee. \'93Tell me where it is. Where is the disc?\'94\
Cracker tried to gargle an answer. Agent Jones released his choke-hold.\
\'93I have no idea what you\'92re talking about,\'94 Cracker pleaded. \
Agent Jones clocked Cracker\'92s head with the butt of his pistol. \'93This is no time for lies.\'94 He clocked Cracker again.\
Cracker protested with cries of agony.\
In the tiny pantry, Sarah found something she could use. She lifted it chin-high and stalked Agent Jones. She was almost there. She hefted the thing above her head like a battle axe.\
\'93Stop,\'94 Agent Jones said as his arm swung and the pistol cocked.\
Sarah was looking straight down an uncaring barrel. On the couch, Cracker twisted his hips and shifted his weight just enough to lever Agent Jones, and his arm, and his hand, and the gun he was holding. Reflexively, Agent Jones pulled the trigger. The bullet struck. Gushing, frothing liquid exploded. Sarah cried out and brought her blunt instrument down upon Agent Jones\'92 head. He crumpled unconscious over Cracker, who made hard work of pushing him aside.\
Sarah froze in the shock of the near miss. Everthing was sticky and wet.\
Cracker smiled and warmed Sarah\'92s reanimation. \'93You know,\'94 he said, \'93you\'92ll have to pay for that case of beer.\'94\
